---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const path = '/terms/';
const title = 'Terms of Service — DQF Expiration Tracker';
const description =
  'Terms for the free DQF Expiration Tracker: service description, no legal advice, local browser data, acceptable use, intellectual property, and limitation of liability.';

import { CANONICAL_ORIGIN } from '../../lib/site';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: CANONICAL_ORIGIN + '/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Terms of Service', item: CANONICAL_ORIGIN + '/terms/' },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Terms of Service — DQF Expiration Tracker',
    url: CANONICAL_ORIGIN + '/terms/',
    inLanguage: 'en',
    isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'DQF Expiration Tracker', url: CANONICAL_ORIGIN + '/' },
  },
];
---

<LegalLayout title={title} description={description} path={path} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <h2>1. Service description</h2>
  <p>
    The DQF Expiration Tracker is a free web tool that calculates estimated next due dates for
    selected driver qualification documents. It supports up to five drivers per browser and covers
    the medical examiner's certificate, MVR pull, CDL expiration, annual review, road test, and
    employment verification. Calculations run in your browser using the dates you enter and your
    device date.
  </p>
  <p>
    This build does not offer payments, PDF exports, email reminders, accounts, cloud sync, or team
    features. Do not rely on a feature that is not visible in the current build.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Not legal advice</h2>
  <p>
    The tracker provides estimates for planning. It is not legal, compliance, or audit advice, and it
    does not guarantee compliance or audit results. Rule references such as 49 CFR 391.45(b) are
    engineering pointers. Regulations and state-issued credentials can change. Verify with FMCSA,
    your state, or a qualified safety consultant before making a compliance decision.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Data and privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Driver labels and dates are stored in your browser's localStorage. They are not uploaded by this
    build. You are responsible for exporting a backup before clearing browser data and for keeping
    the backup file private. Optional first-party analytics record anonymous, aggregated usage
    events only (event names, bucketed counts, page path, device type, referrer host) and never
    driver names, dates, or backup contents; you can reject analytics and keep full functionality.
    The <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> describes storage, analytics consent, deletion, and
    export in more detail.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the browser blocks localStorage, the tracker may operate in memory mode and data will be lost
    when the tab closes. The tracker displays a warning when this happens.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Payments and refunds (future)</h2>
  <p>
    Payments are not available in this build, and no purchase can be made. If paid features are added
    later, the price, tax treatment, and refund policy will be published on a pricing page and in an
    updated version of these terms before any charge is accepted. Nothing in this build creates a
    paid subscription or a refund obligation.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>use the tracker for unlawful purposes or to store data you do not have the right to hold;</li>
    <li>attempt to disrupt, overload, reverse engineer, or bypass the site's security controls;</li>
    <li>scrape or copy the site in a way that degrades service for other users;</li>
    <li>misrepresent the tracker's output as a legal determination or an audit certification.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    The site's text, design, rule table, and code are owned by the site operator or its licensors and
    are provided for your personal or internal business use. The driver data you enter belongs to
    you. Exporting a backup does not transfer ownership of the site's content.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    The tracker is provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, express or
    implied, including fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, or non-infringement. The
    calculation depends on the dates you enter and on your device clock. A wrong input or a wrong
    device date produces a wrong result.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, the site operator is not liable for indirect, incidental,
    special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, lost data, fines, or
    compliance penalties arising from use of or inability to use the tracker. Where liability cannot
    be excluded, it is limited to the amount you paid to use the tracker, which is zero for this
    build.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes and termination</h2>
  <p>
    The operator may change, suspend, or discontinue the tracker or these terms. Material changes
    will be reflected by the "Last updated" date. Continued use after a change means you accept the
    updated terms. If you do not agree, stop using the tracker and delete the local data.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the operator's jurisdiction, without regard to conflict
    of law rules. The specific jurisdiction is a placeholder to be confirmed before launch.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <strong>apj56423@gmail.com</strong>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
